cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Hexapod CPG — Bio-inspired Locomotion on a Custom 18-DoF Robot"
message: "If you reference this code in academic or industrial work, please cite as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Janga
    given-names: Bliss
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end hexapod robotics project: full mechanical CAD, Arduino-Mega
  firmware with IMU heading-hold tripod walking and bump avoidance, and a
  Python central-pattern-generator (CPG) simulation built on a network of
  six Kuramoto-coupled phase oscillators.  Three gait patterns (wave,
  ripple, tripod) emerge from a single parameter (natural frequency ω) and
  the resulting foot trajectories drive a geometry-faithful 18-DoF inverse-
  kinematics solver.  A real-time matplotlib visualiser exposes the dynamics
  of the CPG itself (phase wheel, gait diagram, order parameter) rather than
  only the resulting motion.
keywords:
  - robotics
  - hexapod
  - central-pattern-generator
  - kuramoto
  - coupled-oscillators
  - gait-generation
  - inverse-kinematics
  - arduino
  - imu
  - bioinspired-robotics
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-04-29"
